>
> Hmmm... a person will jairterbe'i even if I give something to him.

Perhaps, or perhaps not. lujvo are not meant to contain full definitions, nor
are they meant to be always guessable at first sight. The precise meaning
of {jairterbe'i} or {tolrenro} (or most lujvo) cannot be determined
from its parts.
If {kavbu} did not exist, one of them or some other could come to mean
"catch" or something similar to "catch". So it could eventually be that
{mi jgari gi'e te benji gi'e nai jairterbe'i}.

